  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The bob of a swinging seconds pendulum (one whose time period is $2 \\mathrm{~s}$ ) has a small speed $\\mathrm{v}_{0}$ at its lowest point. Its height from this lowest point $2.25 \\mathrm{~s}$ after passing through it is given by",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QUu6y",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{0}^{2}}{2 \\mathrm{~g}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2f6po",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{v}_{0}^{2}}{\\mathrm{~g}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3wK1H",
      "text": "$\\frac{v_{0}^{2}}{4 g}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8IXPA",
      "text": "$\\frac{9 v_{0}^{2}}{4 g}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$T=2$ sec.\r\nat $\\mathrm{t}=\\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{T} / 8$\r\n$\\mathrm{t}=\\mathrm{T}+\\mathrm{T} / 8 \\quad \\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{A} \\omega \\cos \\omega \\mathrm{t}=\\mathrm{v}_{0} / \\sqrt{2}$\r\nBy Mechanical energy conservation:\r\n$\\left(\\frac{v_{0}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2}=v_{0}^{2}-2 g h \\quad h=\\frac{v_{0}^{2}}{4 g}$",
    "image": null
